<p>Well written but thoroughly disinteresting. The premise of statues that think independently is a pretty common trope, and I liked what was done here what in terms of the &quot;we live startlingly close to you and we've been coming here for years&quot; but it lacked the shocking twist or at least exotic resolution I anticipated. Don't get me wrong this could be reworked, and by the writing demonstrated in its current state reworked well, but it just couldn't rope me in.</p>

